Now JS update deco text and clock. Add function decoLines and update in updateHUD or showEvent. Use s.beat stable.

Also note `.night-deco` flex grows but if story card tall + deco min 104 exceeds available, story scrolls; fine. On short screens, maybe hide deco under 620 height to preserve space? There's still ~? At 640 height: story area 400, card 300, deco min104 +10 = 414 → scrolls slightly. Better hide deco when viewport height <=680? Use CSS media: `@media (max-height:700px){.night-deco{min-height:70px}}` and `@media (max-height:600px){.night-deco{display:none}}`. Add.

Clock: beginNight s.minutes=0.

Outfit deco update.

Implement:
```js
function decoLine(){
 const lines=[...];
 if (s.smell>=2) return '...';
 ...
 return lines[(s.beat + s.night) % lines.length];
}
```
Set in showEvent and renderResumedEvent after text. Also update in updateHUD? Simpler in showEvent. Deco outfit too.

`decoOutfit` text: `${so.name} · ${sh.name}` uppercase via CSS.

